---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Privacy notice" description="What personal data this site processes when you visit it, why, and what your rights are.">
	<header class="intro">
		<h1>Privacy notice</h1>
	</header>
	<div class="prose">
		<p>
			This notice explains what personal data this site processes and why. It follows the Swiss Federal Act on Data
			Protection (FADP).
		</p>

		<h2>Who is responsible</h2>
		<p>
			Gabriel Torres Gamez<br />
			Email: <a href="mailto:gabriel.torres@fuet.ch">gabriel.torres@fuet.ch</a>
		</p>

		<h2>Server logs and country check</h2>
		<p>When you open a page, the web server records each request:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>your IP address,</li>
			<li>the date and time,</li>
			<li>the page or file you requested and the server's response code,</li>
			<li>
				the browser identification your browser sends (user agent) and the page you came from (referrer), if your
				browser sends them.
			</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			The server also looks up the country of your IP address, on the server itself, and blocks requests from some
			countries to keep unwanted traffic away.
		</p>
		<p>
			I use these logs only to run the site, to find errors, and to detect and stop abuse and attacks. I do not use
			them to build profiles of visitors and do not combine them with other data. The logs are deleted after 7 days.
		</p>

		<h2>No cookies, tracking or third parties</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>The site sets no cookies and uses no analytics, advertising or social media plugins.</li>
			<li>All files (scripts, styles, fonts, images) come from this server. Pages load nothing from other servers.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>Data stored in your browser</h2>
		<p>
			If you pick Light or Dark in the theme switch, the site saves that choice in your browser's local storage under
			the name <code>theme</code>. If you pick Auto, the value is removed. It stays in your browser and is never sent
			to the server.
		</p>
		<p>
			You can delete it at any time by clearing the data of this site in your browser settings. You can also block
			site data for this site. The site still works, but it does not remember your theme.
		</p>

		<h2>Who receives your data</h2>
		<p>
			No one. The site runs on a server in Switzerland. I do not pass log data to third parties and do not send it
			abroad.
		</p>

		<h2>Authors</h2>
		<p>
			Posts show the name of the person who wrote them. If you wrote a post here and want your name changed or
			removed, write to the email address above.
		</p>

		<h2>Links to other websites</h2>
		<p>
			Posts link to other websites. When you follow such a link, the privacy rules of that website apply.
		</p>

		<h2>Your rights</h2>
		<p>
			You can ask which personal data about you I process, and ask me to correct or delete it. Write to the email
			address above. To find log entries about you, I need your IP address and the approximate time of your visit.
		</p>
		<p>
			You can also file a complaint with the
			<a href="https://www.edoeb.admin.ch/en">Federal Data Protection and Information Commissioner (FDPIC)</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Changes</h2>
		<p>I may update this notice when the site changes. The current version is always on this page.</p>
		<p>Last updated: 2026-11-11</p>
	</div>
</Base>
